WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.503
The only real sports are
auto racing, bullfighting,

00:00:02.503 --> 00:00:03.420
and mountain climbing.

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:04.628
The rest are just games.

00:00:04.628 --> 00:00:05.670
Never heard that one.

00:00:05.670 --> 00:00:06.250
 You never heard that?

00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:07.110
Classic Hemingway.

00:00:07.110 --> 00:00:08.152
You've got to use that.

00:00:08.152 --> 00:00:09.390
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:12.390
We have a combined 60 years
of rock climbing experience

00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:14.955
at an elite level.

00:00:14.955 --> 00:00:20.040
The Dawn Wall was my quest to
really find my physical limits.

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:23.220
It's still considered the
hardest big-wall free-climb

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:24.900
in the world.

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:26.790
Free solo climbing
means climbing

00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:28.200
with no rope to protect you.

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:31.110
The fact that he was the
first one to free solo El Cap

00:00:31.110 --> 00:00:32.409
was such a big deal.

00:00:32.409 --> 00:00:36.482
People didn't think that it
would ever get free soloed.

00:00:36.482 --> 00:00:38.190
 The lessons that
you take from climbing

00:00:38.190 --> 00:00:40.680
around success and failure
helps put the rest of life

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:42.990
in perspective.

00:00:42.990 --> 00:00:44.910
Climbing is like a fine
spice that brings out

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:48.490
the flavor of the rest of life.

00:00:48.490 --> 00:00:51.280
We have spent quite a bit of
time refining our own climbing.

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:53.740
And we are happy to share
that knowledge with anybody

00:00:53.740 --> 00:00:55.810
who's interested in the sport.

00:00:55.810 --> 00:00:58.660
 Footwork is generally the
most important part of climbing.

00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:00.370
It all looks horrendously
uncomfortable.

00:01:00.370 --> 00:01:01.600
But you get used to it.

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:04.090
The point of using your
arms in rock climbing

00:01:04.090 --> 00:01:05.680
is to keep you
balanced over your feet

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:08.080
so that your feet can
push you up the wall.

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:11.050
 98% of bouldering
is just falling off.

00:01:11.050 --> 00:01:12.040
Falling over and over.

00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:13.480
You're just like
[GROANS] This is actually

00:01:13.480 --> 00:01:15.897
a perfect example of where
technique matters because right

00:01:15.897 --> 00:01:17.530
now I'm hanging
off two holds, kind

00:01:17.530 --> 00:01:18.798
of strenuous on the fingers.

00:01:18.798 --> 00:01:21.340
But instead, I can lean in and
push my knee against the wall.

00:01:21.340 --> 00:01:22.810
Look, I can suddenly
go no hands.

00:01:22.810 --> 00:01:25.930
We also sprinkle in a little
bit of the psychological aspects

00:01:25.930 --> 00:01:26.635
of the sport.

00:01:26.635 --> 00:01:28.660
And how to not
look like a Gumby.

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:30.425
It's a fun term for a beginner.

00:01:30.425 --> 00:01:32.800
If you're wearing your climbing
shoes in the parking lot,

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:33.508
you're Gumby-ing.

00:01:36.220 --> 00:01:38.830
Climbing is a really incredible
way to connect with nature.

00:01:38.830 --> 00:01:41.570
[SCREAMING] All of my
craziest experiences,

00:01:41.570 --> 00:01:44.480
all my hardest experiences,
all my best experiences

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:46.910
are all associated
with climbing.

00:01:46.910 --> 00:01:48.593
I've made pretty
intentional choices

00:01:48.593 --> 00:01:49.760
with the way I lead my life.

00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:52.518
I welcome anybody
else to do the same.

00:01:52.518 --> 00:01:53.810
That doesn't mean to free solo.

00:01:53.810 --> 00:01:55.643
I mean to think about
their life critically.

00:01:55.643 --> 00:01:56.594
[LAUGHTER]

00:01:58.000 --> 00:01:59.050
 I'm Tommy Caldwell.

00:01:59.050 --> 00:02:00.160
 And I'm Alex Honnold.

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:01.087
 And this--

00:02:01.087 --> 00:02:02.170
BOTH: --is my MasterClass.

00:02:02.170 --> 00:02:03.170
 We've totally [BLEEP].

00:02:03.170 --> 00:02:04.390
 I'm Tommy Caldwell.

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:05.560
 And I'm Alex Honnold.

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:07.480
BOTH: And this is MasterClass.

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:10.474
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:02:13.470 --> 00:02:16.400
 MasterClass, don't be a Gumby.

